# Airsup isolation

`/airsup` is a standalone slice. Keep it easy to delete.

## Put Airsup code only in
- `airsup/` (routes, views, db, sql, public, revert)
- the marked `AIRSUP-BEGIN` / `AIRSUP-END` blocks in `server/server.js`
- `"airsup/**"` in `vercel.json` includeFiles

## Do not
- Import `server/db/supabase.js`, diary routes, or admin routes from Airsup
- Add Airsup links, buttons, or data to other pages
- Put Airsup styles in `public/css/style.css` — use `airsup/public/` instead
- Share tables with the rest of the site — use `airsup_*` tables only
- Fake a Gmail login. Real Google OAuth only (`AIRSUP_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID` / `AIRSUP_GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET`)
- Hardcode Tade (or anyone) as a match. ChatGPT finds people with `find_people` on the Airsup MCP
- Hold listing answers out of the directory. Every onboarding question is listed
- Use Gmail as the conversation. Gmail is only a wake from `tademehl@gmail.com` with `[AIRSUP]`

## Live
MCP URL is always `https://www.tademehl.com/airsup/mcp`. Tools: `find_people`, `send_message`, `end_conversation`. Caller identity is plugin OAuth. `send_message.person_id` is the recipient. Wake mail is a separate `gmail.send` grant for `tademehl@gmail.com` using the existing Google callback `/airsup/auth/google/callback`.

ChatGPT conversation UI is a widget resource (`ui://widget/airsup-conversation-v2.html`) attached in `_meta` on `send_message` and `end_conversation`. CSP and unique `openai/widgetDomain` live on the resource `_meta`, not in the locked tool JSON. Transcript, other party, and thread list go in tool-result `_meta.ui.panel` and the authenticated `airsup://conversations` resource. Do not add a fourth tool. Do not put extra fields in `structuredContent`. The widget calls `send_message` and `end_conversation` through `tools/call`.

## Endpoint prompt (Gmail-woken ChatGPT)

The callee worker is instructed with the verbatim text in `airsup/prompts/endpoint-gmail-trigger.txt`. That is the ChatGPT Gmail-trigger **Instructions** block. Do not paraphrase it. `/airsup/prompt` copies that file, then adds the trigger filter: new mail from `tademehl@gmail.com` whose subject contains `[AIRSUP]`.

## Revert
```bash
node airsup/revert-airsup.js
```
See `airsup/REVERT.md`.
